#ifndef __ASTROPOP_GAMETEXT_H__
#define __ASTROPOP_GAMETEXT_H__

// The texts AstroPop shows (dialogs, story and help screens, tutorial boxes, labels) are hard-coded in the
// original's exe; there is no string file. port: by the user's decision (2026-10-19) no game text is in the
// repository: the port reads every text at start-up from the player's own executable, by address, and a mod or
// language pack can replace any of them.
//
// - GameTextTable.inc (generated by games/astropop/tools/make_gametext.py) lists each string's address in
//   the 1.0 game image, its length and a hash: no text.
// - LoadGameTexts() finds WinAP.exe in the game folder (the Steam copy's launcher with the game image after PopCap's
//   marker; a carved AstroPopGame.exe works too, and so does AstroPop.exe, the game of the PopCap Game Collection),
//   reads each text at its address and checks length and hash. The Collection's exe is another build (2007): its
//   texts are the same at other addresses, so a text that is not at its address is looked up by content (length and
//   hash). A text that is nowhere in the exe stays empty and is logged.
// - Code names a text by its address in the original: GT(0x0050b4a4). Overrides: any string property named
//   GT_<8 hex digits> (e.g. <String id="GT_0050b4a4">...</String> in properties/texts.xml, from the game folder
//   or a mod) replaces the text read from the exe.

#include "Common.h"

namespace Sexy
{

// Reads the texts from the game folder's executable and applies the string-property overrides. Returns
// false when the executable is missing or no text matched (the texts are then empty or overrides only).
bool				LoadGameTexts();
// The text the original keeps at theVA; "" for an address that is not in the table
const SexyString&	GameText(unsigned int theVA);

#define GT(theVA) (::Sexy::GameText(theVA))
#define GTC(theVA) (::Sexy::GameText(theVA).c_str())

}

#endif
